			<div class="content" id="post-content-4845208">
									

<p>I like the suggestion of using neutrinos, as they seem to be the closest real-world equivalent to 'incorporeal energy'. As for the fading intangibility I am considering a concept of 'neutrino diffusion', similar to 'hume diffusion' in <a href="/scp-3001">SCP-3001</a> and <a href="/scp-4903">SCP-4903</a>, wherein the intangibility is slowly being shared between the incorporeal objects and earths inner core. This would lead to a sudden absence of the inner core, causing a much more disastrous collapse than would happen if the inner core were replaced with corpses. This would also solve the debate of whether the re-materializing object would replace the solid matter or the other way round. What do you think?</p>

							</div>

								
					
