			<div class="content" id="post-content-4859132">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Given that the agents are all essentially blind, deaf and mute, they communicate with the foundation through an incorporeal computer that fell with them.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>How does the computer communicate from the center of the earth? I honestly can't imagine just handwaving this sorta thing&#8230; how does a signal travel from an incorporeal electronic device to physical electronic devices, through miles and miles of solid mass?</em></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Why are there so many bodies down there?</strong> Like what is happening to make this occur? I can't imagine people are being turned incorporeal this often&#8230; <strong>If they are, why isn't that the SCP and not the bodies at the center of the earth?</strong></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>If the agents are deaf, dumb and blind (<em>I don't know why because the post doesn't say, but I assume because of their status deep in the earth</em>)&#8230; how can they tell the Foundation anything? They have no sensation (<em>because tactile is out, due to their incorporeality</em>)</li>
</ul>
<p>I still think there isn't much to this narrative. It feels like a description of people suffering&#8230; but what is the arc here? Just &quot;we're intangible, and at the center of the earth!&quot; and then dying? (<em>also how would the agents even know about that they're in the center of the earth?</em>)</p>

							</div>

								
					
